        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">How much are generators</strong> in practice? About $400 to $900 for a capable open-frame, $400 to $1,800 for most inverters, $4,000 and up for a diesel portable, and $6,500 to $15,000 or more for an installed standby. The connection, cords, permit and fuel commonly add $100 to $2,000 to a portable, and that is the part most budgets forget.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Compare on cost per running watt, not peak watts, buy the size your real load needs, insist on CO shutoff, and price the house connection before you choose the generator. For most homeowners, a mid-size portable with a 240V outlet and a properly installed inlet and interlock is the best value in home backup power.
          </p>
